//
// A CONVERSION BETWEEN TWO FOREIGN TYPES IS REFUSED (`@FR-Op-Conv` crossed with `@FR-Op-Home`).
// `text → OcPt`: the `self` is built in and the target is another library's, so neither end is a
// type of this source — Op-Conv's exception (a conversion INTO this source's type) does not apply
// and Op-Home refuses the definition where it is written, whatever uses it.
//
// @falsified-at: none — a conformance guard; refused as the rule says, interpret and native.
// CHANNEL: the compile (the expected diagnostic).
// ARMED: no instrument.
// WITNESS: the diagnostic names both types.
// HOLDS: `a-conversion-into-a-type-of-this-source-takes-any-self` beside it.
// @EXPECT_ERROR: `operator to_oc_pt` converts `text` to `OcPt`, and neither is a type of this package

use op_conv_fixture_lib::*;

operator to_oc_pt(self: text) -> OcPt { OcPt { x: len(self), y: 0 } }

fn main() {
  println("x");
}
